rmland-atlas/kansas/gray-county"],["ARC or PLC in Gray County","/arc-plc/kansas/gray-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, February to March and March to April each came in under 90% of normal in 41 of the 75 years from 1951 to 2025 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids. In 2026 so far, the middle of the grids got 9% of normal in February to March and 13% in March to April, then 125% in May to June. Every grid on the page had its driest year in 1956, with grid 20818 at 33% of normal that year.</p>"}
